// ASAA Templates — relational model (US-A01/A02, US-C01/C02/C04, US-D01/D02, US-I02/I03).
// Schema changes are made only through Prisma migrations (apps/api/prisma/migrations).

generator client {
  provider = "prisma-client-js"
}

datasource db {
  provider = "postgresql"
  url      = env("DATABASE_URL")
}

enum OwnerRole {
  OWNER
  ADMIN
  DEVELOPER
  TESTER
  EMPLOYEE
}

/// Account principal retained under the historical Owner model name.
/// Multiple members are supported; only one OWNER is permitted by the database.
model Owner {
  id                        String               @id @default(uuid()) @db.Uuid
  email                     String               @unique @db.VarChar(254)
  displayName               String               @db.VarChar(120)
  role                      OwnerRole            @default(EMPLOYEE)
  isActive                  Boolean              @default(true)
  passwordHash              String               @db.VarChar(512)
  passwordChangedAt         DateTime             @default(now()) @db.Timestamptz(3)
  createdAt                 DateTime             @default(now()) @db.Timestamptz(3)
  /// AES-256-GCM encrypted TOTP secret; pending until mfaEnabledAt is set (US-A04).
  mfaSecretEnc              String?              @db.VarChar(512)
  mfaEnabledAt              DateTime?            @db.Timestamptz(3)
  /// SHA-256 hashes of unused single-use recovery codes.
  mfaRecoveryHashes         String[]             @default([])
  /// Last accepted TOTP time step; codes at or below it are rejected (replay protection).
  mfaLastStep               Int?
  sessions                  Session[]
  projects                  Project[]
  savedSearches             SavedSearch[]
  reviewedAccessRequests    AccessRequest[]      @relation("AccessRequestReviewer")
  projectMemberships        ProjectMember[]
  projectComments           ProjectComment[]     @relation("CommentAuthor")
  resolvedComments          ProjectComment[]     @relation("CommentResolver")
  presence                  ProjectPresence[]
  passwordResetTokens       PasswordResetToken[] @relation("PasswordResetOwner")
  issuedPasswordResetTokens PasswordResetToken[] @relation("PasswordResetIssuer")
}

/// Server-side session. Only a SHA-256 of the opaque cookie token is stored.
model Session {
  id         String    @id @default(uuid()) @db.Uuid
  ownerId    String    @db.Uuid
  owner      Owner     @relation(fields: [ownerId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)
  tokenHash  String    @unique @db.Char(64)
  createdAt  DateTime  @default(now()) @db.Timestamptz(3)
  lastSeenAt DateTime  @default(now()) @db.Timestamptz(3)
  expiresAt  DateTime  @db.Timestamptz(3)
  revokedAt  DateTime? @db.Timestamptz(3)
  userAgent  String?   @db.VarChar(200)

  @@index([ownerId, revokedAt])
}

/// Single-use password recovery token. Only its SHA-256 hash is stored.
model PasswordResetToken {
  id         String    @id @default(uuid()) @db.Uuid
  ownerId    String    @db.Uuid
  owner      Owner     @relation("PasswordResetOwner", fields: [ownerId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)
  issuedById String    @db.Uuid
  issuedBy   Owner     @relation("PasswordResetIssuer", fields: [issuedById], references: [id], onDelete: Restrict)
  tokenHash  String    @unique @db.Char(64)
  createdAt  DateTime  @default(now()) @db.Timestamptz(3)
  expiresAt  DateTime  @db.Timestamptz(3)
  consumedAt DateTime? @db.Timestamptz(3)

  @@index([ownerId, consumedAt, expiresAt])
}

enum AuditActorType {
  OWNER
  MEMBER
  SYSTEM
  ANONYMOUS
}

enum AuditOutcome {
  SUCCESS
  FAILURE
  DENIED
}

/// Append-only audit trail. A database trigger (see migration) rejects UPDATE and DELETE.
model AuditEvent {
  id         BigInt         @id @default(autoincrement())
  at         DateTime       @default(now()) @db.Timestamptz(3)
  actorType  AuditActorType
  actorId    String?        @db.Uuid
  action     String         @db.VarChar(80)
  targetType String?        @db.VarChar(40)
  targetId   String?        @db.VarChar(80)
  outcome    AuditOutcome
  requestId  String?        @db.VarChar(64)
  metadata   Json           @default("{}")

  @@index([at])
  @@index([action])
  @@index([targetType, targetId])
}

enum ProjectStatus {
  PLANNING
  ACTIVE
  ON_HOLD
  COMPLETED
}

model Project {
  id             String              @id @default(uuid()) @db.Uuid
  /// Selected project architecture, captured from the approved starter/template blueprint.
  blueprint      Json?
  key            String              @unique @db.VarChar(20)
  name           String              @db.VarChar(120)
  purpose        String              @default("") @db.VarChar(2000)
  status         ProjectStatus       @default(PLANNING)
  ownerId        String              @db.Uuid
  owner          Owner               @relation(fields: [ownerId], references: [id], onDelete: Restrict)
  archivedAt     DateTime?           @db.Timestamptz(3)
  createdAt      DateTime            @default(now()) @db.Timestamptz(3)
  updatedAt      DateTime            @updatedAt @db.Timestamptz(3)
  /// Optimistic-concurrency version, incremented on every update.
  version        Int                 @default(1)
  /// Next per-project requirement number (REQ-1, REQ-2, ...).
  requirementSeq Int                 @default(0)
  requirements   Requirement[]
  members        ProjectMember[]
  generation     ProjectGeneration?
  executionJobs  ExecutionJob[]
  repository     ProjectRepository?
  environment    ProjectEnvironment?
  comments       ProjectComment[]
  presence       ProjectPresence[]
  deliveries     DeliveryRequest[]

  @@index([ownerId, archivedAt])
}

enum ProjectAccessRole {
  VIEWER
  EDITOR
}

/// Explicit per-project membership. Owner remains the ultimate project administrator.
model ProjectMember {
  id        String            @id @default(uuid()) @db.Uuid
  projectId String            @db.Uuid
  project   Project           @relation(fields: [projectId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)
  memberId  String            @db.Uuid
  member    Owner             @relation(fields: [memberId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)
  role      ProjectAccessRole @default(VIEWER)
  createdAt DateTime          @default(now()) @db.Timestamptz(3)
  updatedAt DateTime          @updatedAt @db.Timestamptz(3)

  @@unique([projectId, memberId])
  @@index([memberId, projectId])
}

enum RequirementKind {
  REQUIREMENT
  USER_STORY
}

enum Priority {
  P0
  P1
  P2
}

enum RequirementStatus {
  DRAFT
  READY
  IN_DEVELOPMENT
  DEVELOPED
  BUILT
  TESTED
  RELEASED
}

model Requirement {
  id                 String                  @id @default(uuid()) @db.Uuid
  projectId          String                  @db.Uuid
  project            Project                 @relation(fields: [projectId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)
  code               String                  @db.VarChar(20)
  kind               RequirementKind         @default(USER_STORY)
  title              String                  @db.VarChar(200)
  description        String                  @default("") @db.VarChar(5000)
  priority           Priority                @default(P1)
  status             RequirementStatus       @default(DRAFT)
  acceptanceCriteria String[]                @default([])
  flaggedForReview   Boolean                 @default(false)
  flagReason         String?                 @db.VarChar(500)
  version            Int                     @default(1)
  createdAt          DateTime                @default(now()) @db.Timestamptz(3)
  updatedAt          DateTime                @updatedAt @db.Timestamptz(3)
  dependsOn          RequirementDependency[] @relation("dependent")
  dependedOnBy       RequirementDependency[] @relation("dependency")
  versions           RequirementVersion[]
  links              TraceLink[]

  @@unique([projectId, code])
  @@index([projectId, status])
}

/// Dependencies are restricted to the same project by the service layer (US-I03).
model RequirementDependency {
  requirementId String      @db.Uuid
  dependsOnId   String      @db.Uuid
  requirement   Requirement @relation("dependent", fields: [requirementId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)
  dependsOn     Requirement @relation("dependency", fields: [dependsOnId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)

  @@id([requirementId, dependsOnId])
}

/// Immutable snapshot of every requirement version (US-C02 traceable changes).
model RequirementVersion {
  id            String      @id @default(uuid()) @db.Uuid
  requirementId String      @db.Uuid
  requirement   Requirement @relation(fields: [requirementId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)
  version       Int
  snapshot      Json
  changeNote    String?     @db.VarChar(300)
  changedAt     DateTime    @default(now()) @db.Timestamptz(3)

  @@unique([requirementId, version])
}

enum TraceKind {
  TASK
  CODE_CHANGE
  TEST
  DEFECT
  DOCUMENTATION
  RELEASE
}

enum EvidenceStatus {
  PLANNED
  PASSED
  FAILED
}

/// Requirement → delivery traceability (US-C04).
model TraceLink {
  id             String         @id @default(uuid()) @db.Uuid
  requirementId  String         @db.Uuid
  requirement    Requirement    @relation(fields: [requirementId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)
  kind           TraceKind
  reference      String         @db.VarChar(300)
  title          String?        @db.VarChar(200)
  evidenceStatus EvidenceStatus @default(PLANNED)
  createdAt      DateTime       @default(now()) @db.Timestamptz(3)

  @@index([requirementId, kind])
}

enum CatalogKind {
  TEMPLATE
  COMPONENT
  DESIGN_ASSET
  WORKFLOW
  IMPORTED_PROJECT
}

enum Lifecycle {
  DRAFT
  ACTIVE
  DEPRECATED
  RETIRED
}

enum TrustStatus {
  UNTRUSTED
  UNDER_REVIEW
  TRUSTED
}

enum SourceType {
  AUTHORED
  IMPORTED
}

/// Private catalog of reusable templates and assets (US-D01, US-D02).
model CatalogItem {
  id                    String              @id @default(uuid()) @db.Uuid
  slug                  String              @unique @db.VarChar(80)
  title                 String              @db.VarChar(160)
  description           String              @default("") @db.VarChar(4000)
  kind                  CatalogKind         @default(TEMPLATE)
  category              String              @db.VarChar(80)
  technologies          String[]            @default([])
  tags                  String[]            @default([])
  version               String              @db.VarChar(40)
  lifecycle             Lifecycle           @default(DRAFT)
  trustStatus           TrustStatus         @default(TRUSTED)
  sourceType            SourceType          @default(AUTHORED)
  sourceReference       String?             @db.VarChar(500)
  license               String              @db.VarChar(80)
  ownership             String              @db.VarChar(120)
  dependencies          Json                @default("[]")
  /// Library template id whose content this record approves for generation (US-E01).
  contentRef            String?             @db.VarChar(80)
  /// SHA-256 of the approved template content; generation refuses any other content.
  contentDigest         String?             @db.Char(64)
  /// Business sector this asset is organised under (taxonomy SECTOR term key); null means cross-sector.
  sector                String?             @db.VarChar(80)
  metadataSchemaVersion Int                 @default(1)
  createdAt             DateTime            @default(now()) @db.Timestamptz(3)
  updatedAt             DateTime            @updatedAt @db.Timestamptz(3)
  rowVersion            Int                 @default(1)
  generations           ProjectGeneration[]

  @@index([category])
  @@index([lifecycle])
  @@index([sector])
}

enum GenerationMode {
  SCRATCH
  TEMPLATE
}

enum GenerationStatus {
  PENDING
  SUCCEEDED
  FAILED
}

/// Record of how a project's independent output was generated (US-E01, US-E02).
/// Kept separate from reusable template definitions: it stores the exact template
/// id, version and content digest used, the validated inputs and the output digest.
model ProjectGeneration {
  id               String           @id @default(uuid()) @db.Uuid
  projectId        String           @unique @db.Uuid
  project          Project          @relation(fields: [projectId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)
  mode             GenerationMode
  status           GenerationStatus @default(PENDING)
  templateId       String           @db.VarChar(80)
  templateVersion  String           @db.VarChar(40)
  templateDigest   String           @db.Char(64)
  catalogItemId    String?          @db.Uuid
  catalogItem      CatalogItem?     @relation(fields: [catalogItemId], references: [id], onDelete: SetNull)
  generatorVersion String           @db.VarChar(20)
  inputs           Json             @default("{}")
  requirements     String[]         @default([])
  inputsHash       String           @db.Char(64)
  /// Output folder name under the generation root; unique so outputs never collide.
  outputDir        String           @unique @db.VarChar(80)
  outputDigest     String?          @db.Char(64)
  files            String[]         @default([])
  attempts         Int              @default(1)
  error            String?          @db.VarChar(500)
  startedAt        DateTime         @default(now()) @db.Timestamptz(3)
  completedAt      DateTime?        @db.Timestamptz(3)
  version          Int              @default(1)

  @@index([status])
  @@index([catalogItemId])
}

enum RepositoryProviderKind {
  LOCAL_GIT
  GITHUB
  GITLAB
  BITBUCKET
}

/// Source-control metadata for a generated project (US-F01, US-F02). Provider
/// credentials are never stored here; remotes are recorded, not synchronised.
model ProjectRepository {
  id              String                 @id @default(uuid()) @db.Uuid
  projectId       String                 @unique @db.Uuid
  project         Project                @relation(fields: [projectId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)
  provider        RepositoryProviderKind @default(LOCAL_GIT)
  defaultBranch   String                 @db.VarChar(100)
  /// Branching policy (production/integration/work prefixes, protected branches).
  policy          Json
  identityName    String                 @db.VarChar(100)
  identityEmail   String                 @db.VarChar(254)
  remoteName      String?                @db.VarChar(40)
  remoteUrl       String?                @db.VarChar(500)
  adoptedExisting Boolean                @default(false)
  initializedAt   DateTime               @default(now()) @db.Timestamptz(3)
  updatedAt       DateTime               @updatedAt @db.Timestamptz(3)
  version         Int                    @default(1)
}

/// Reproducible development environment specification (US-F03). Holds tool
/// versions, commands and variable names/descriptions only, never secret values.
model ProjectEnvironment {
  id        String   @id @default(uuid()) @db.Uuid
  projectId String   @unique @db.Uuid
  project   Project  @relation(fields: [projectId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)
  spec      Json
  createdAt DateTime @default(now()) @db.Timestamptz(3)
  updatedAt DateTime @updatedAt @db.Timestamptz(3)
  version   Int      @default(1)
}

/// Private saved search definitions. Each record belongs to exactly one owner.
model SavedSearch {
  id        String   @id @default(uuid()) @db.Uuid
  ownerId   String   @db.Uuid
  owner     Owner    @relation(fields: [ownerId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)
  name      String   @db.VarChar(100)
  query     String   @db.VarChar(80)
  filters   Json     @default("{}")
  createdAt DateTime @default(now()) @db.Timestamptz(3)
  updatedAt DateTime @updatedAt @db.Timestamptz(3)

  @@unique([ownerId, name])
  @@index([ownerId, updatedAt])
}

enum AccessRequestStatus {
  PENDING
  APPROVED
  REJECTED
}

/// Public employee access request; activation secrets are stored only as hashes.
model AccessRequest {
  id             String              @id @default(uuid()) @db.Uuid
  email          String              @db.VarChar(254)
  displayName    String              @db.VarChar(120)
  reason         String              @default("") @db.VarChar(1000)
  status         AccessRequestStatus @default(PENDING)
  approvedRole   OwnerRole           @default(EMPLOYEE)
  tokenHash      String?             @unique @db.Char(64)
  tokenExpiresAt DateTime?           @db.Timestamptz(3)
  activatedAt    DateTime?           @db.Timestamptz(3)
  reviewerId     String?             @db.Uuid
  reviewer       Owner?              @relation("AccessRequestReviewer", fields: [reviewerId], references: [id], onDelete: SetNull)
  reviewedAt     DateTime?           @db.Timestamptz(3)
  createdAt      DateTime            @default(now()) @db.Timestamptz(3)
  updatedAt      DateTime            @updatedAt @db.Timestamptz(3)

  @@index([status, createdAt])
  @@index([email, status])
}

enum ReleaseStatus {
  DRAFT
  IN_REVIEW
  APPROVED
  RELEASED
  DEPRECATED
}

/// Version ledger for library templates (RG-06): draft -> review -> approved -> released (immutable) -> deprecated.
/// Released rows can never change identity, digest or manifest; the database enforces this with a trigger.
model TemplateRelease {
  id                String        @id @default(uuid()) @db.Uuid
  templateId        String        @db.VarChar(80)
  version           String        @db.VarChar(40)
  status            ReleaseStatus @default(DRAFT)
  /// SHA-256 of the library content captured when the draft was created.
  contentDigest     String        @db.Char(64)
  /// Snapshot of the validated manifest at draft time.
  manifest          Json
  notes             String        @default("") @db.VarChar(500)
  reviewNote        String        @default("") @db.VarChar(500)
  createdById       String        @db.Uuid
  submittedById     String?       @db.Uuid
  approvedById      String?       @db.Uuid
  releasedById      String?       @db.Uuid
  createdAt         DateTime      @default(now()) @db.Timestamptz(3)
  submittedAt       DateTime?     @db.Timestamptz(3)
  approvedAt        DateTime?     @db.Timestamptz(3)
  releasedAt        DateTime?     @db.Timestamptz(3)
  deprecatedAt      DateTime?     @db.Timestamptz(3)
  deprecationReason String?       @db.VarChar(500)
  replacedByVersion String?       @db.VarChar(40)
  rowVersion        Int           @default(1)

  @@unique([templateId, version])
  @@index([status])
}

/// Shared fixed-window rate-limit counters (replaces per-process memory so limits survive restarts and span instances).
model RateLimitBucket {
  key     String   @id @db.VarChar(240)
  count   Int
  resetAt DateTime @db.Timestamptz(3)

  @@index([resetAt])
}

enum ExecutionJobStatus {
  QUEUED
  RUNNING
  SUCCEEDED
  FAILED
  CANCELLED
  TIMED_OUT
  LIMIT_EXCEEDED
}

/// Build/test job executed by the isolated worker against a disposable copy of a project folder.
model ExecutionJob {
  id            String             @id @default(uuid()) @db.Uuid
  projectId     String             @db.Uuid
  project       Project            @relation(fields: [projectId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)
  requestedById String             @db.Uuid
  task          String             @db.VarChar(40)
  target        String             @default("") @db.VarChar(240)
  isolation     String             @db.VarChar(20)
  status        ExecutionJobStatus @default(QUEUED)
  exitCode      Int?
  stdout        String             @default("") @db.Text
  stderr        String             @default("") @db.Text
  truncated     Boolean            @default(false)
  reason        String?            @db.VarChar(300)
  createdAt     DateTime           @default(now()) @db.Timestamptz(3)
  startedAt     DateTime?          @db.Timestamptz(3)
  finishedAt    DateTime?          @db.Timestamptz(3)

  @@index([projectId, createdAt])
  @@index([status])
}

enum CommentTarget {
  PROJECT
  TEMPLATE
  FILE
}

/// Threaded comment on a project, a template version or a workspace file. Deleting keeps the thread shape (soft delete).
model ProjectComment {
  id           String           @id @default(uuid()) @db.Uuid
  projectId    String           @db.Uuid
  project      Project          @relation(fields: [projectId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)
  targetType   CommentTarget
  /// File path, template id@version, or empty for the project itself.
  targetRef    String           @default("") @db.VarChar(300)
  parentId     String?          @db.Uuid
  parent       ProjectComment?  @relation("CommentThread", fields: [parentId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)
  replies      ProjectComment[] @relation("CommentThread")
  authorId     String           @db.Uuid
  author       Owner            @relation("CommentAuthor", fields: [authorId], references: [id], onDelete: Restrict)
  body         String           @db.VarChar(4000)
  /// Member ids mentioned in the body (project members only).
  mentions     String[]         @default([])
  createdAt    DateTime         @default(now()) @db.Timestamptz(3)
  editedAt     DateTime?        @db.Timestamptz(3)
  deletedAt    DateTime?        @db.Timestamptz(3)
  resolvedAt   DateTime?        @db.Timestamptz(3)
  resolvedById String?          @db.Uuid
  resolvedBy   Owner?           @relation("CommentResolver", fields: [resolvedById], references: [id], onDelete: SetNull)

  @@index([projectId, targetType, targetRef, createdAt])
  @@index([parentId])
}

enum PresenceMode {
  VIEWING
  EDITING
}

/// Heartbeat-based presence: one current location per member per project.
model ProjectPresence {
  projectId String       @db.Uuid
  project   Project      @relation(fields: [projectId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)
  memberId  String       @db.Uuid
  member    Owner        @relation(fields: [memberId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)
  filePath  String       @default("") @db.VarChar(400)
  mode      PresenceMode @default(VIEWING)
  seenAt    DateTime     @default(now()) @db.Timestamptz(3)

  @@id([projectId, memberId])
  @@index([projectId, seenAt])
}

enum AsaaEventStatus {
  PENDING
  DELIVERED
  DEAD
}

/// Durable outbox for ASAA ecosystem events (asaa.event.v1). The row id is the envelope id (idempotency key).
/// The envelope never contains secrets, file contents or paths; lastError holds an HTTP status or error class only.
model AsaaEventOutbox {
  id            String          @id @db.Uuid
  type          String          @db.VarChar(80)
  envelope      Json
  status        AsaaEventStatus @default(PENDING)
  attempts      Int             @default(0)
  nextAttemptAt DateTime        @default(now()) @db.Timestamptz(3)
  deliveredAt   DateTime?       @db.Timestamptz(3)
  lastError     String?         @db.VarChar(120)
  createdAt     DateTime        @default(now()) @db.Timestamptz(3)

  @@index([status, nextAttemptAt])
  @@index([status, createdAt])
}

enum DeliveryKind {
  ZIP_EXPORT
  WORKSPACE_EXPORT
  REPOSITORY_HANDOFF
  DEPLOYMENT
}

enum DeliveryStatus {
  REQUESTED
  EXECUTED
  REJECTED
  FAILED
  CANCELLED
}

/// Permission and audit ledger for everything that leaves a project: ZIP/workspace exports, repository
/// handoff and deployment. Handoff and deployment need a management decision; exports need explicit confirmation.
model DeliveryRequest {
  id            String         @id @default(uuid()) @db.Uuid
  projectId     String         @db.Uuid
  project       Project        @relation(fields: [projectId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)
  kind          DeliveryKind
  status        DeliveryStatus @default(REQUESTED)
  /// Provider id (local implementation ids only unless an owner-approved adapter is registered).
  provider      String         @db.VarChar(40)
  /// Repository name or deployment environment; empty for exports.
  target        String         @default("") @db.VarChar(120)
  note          String         @default("") @db.VarChar(500)
  requestedById String         @db.Uuid
  decidedById   String?        @db.Uuid
  decisionNote  String         @default("") @db.VarChar(500)
  /// Provider result (locations, digests); never secrets.
  result        Json?
  createdAt     DateTime       @default(now()) @db.Timestamptz(3)
  decidedAt     DateTime?      @db.Timestamptz(3)
  executedAt    DateTime?      @db.Timestamptz(3)

  @@index([projectId, createdAt])
  @@index([status, kind])
}

enum TaxonomyKind {
  CATEGORY
  SECTOR
}

/// Managed vocabulary for the catalogue: categories and business sectors, each with an optional steward.
model TaxonomyTerm {
  id          String       @id @default(uuid()) @db.Uuid
  kind        TaxonomyKind
  key         String       @db.VarChar(80)
  label       String       @db.VarChar(120)
  description String       @default("") @db.VarChar(500)
  parentKey   String?      @db.VarChar(80)
  /// Owner (member) accountable for assets in this term; not a foreign key so member removal never blocks admin.
  stewardId   String?      @db.Uuid
  active      Boolean      @default(true)
  createdAt   DateTime     @default(now()) @db.Timestamptz(3)
  updatedAt   DateTime     @updatedAt @db.Timestamptz(3)
  rowVersion  Int          @default(1)

  @@unique([kind, key])
}

/// Durable connector revocations (D3.20). One-way: a row means the connector and its credential are never reusable.
model ConnectorRevocation {
  connectorId String   @id @db.VarChar(40)
  revokedById String?  @db.Uuid
  revokedAt   DateTime @default(now()) @db.Timestamptz(3)
}
